#N canvas 20 20 1750 1400 12;
#X text 20 20 g_oled -- the display arbiter. Four layers with priority and a time to live: home < param < modal < alert. Callers push semantics onto the disp bus whenever they have something to say \; the screen redraws on its own clock and shows whichever layer is winning., f 58;
#X text 20 130 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 175 SOLE OWNER OF THE SCREEN. Nothing else in Cut It may send on oscOut or screenLine1-5 -- including u_err \, which forwards onto disp and lets this file decide what an error looks like., f 58;
#X text 20 265 LAYERS ARE STATE \, NOT DRAW CALLS. Every layer keeps its values and the frame clock renders whichever one wins. That is why there is no rate limiting anywhere: the last value written is what the next frame draws \, so 200 messages a second and one every five seconds both come out as ten frames a second \, and neither can strand a stale half-swept value on the screen., f 58;
#N canvas 30 30 1900 800 disp-in 0;
#X text 20 20 THE RESERVED SELECTORS ARE THIS ROUTE BOX. in-l \, in-r and status feed the home screen \; modal \, modal-off and alert name a layer directly. EVERYTHING ELSE FALLS OUT OF THE REJECT OUTLET AND IS A PARAMETER., f 58;
#X text 20 115 Callers never say which layer they want -- see ref-conventions.md \, The display bus. A mistyped disp name shows up on the screen as a nonsense parameter \, which is a great deal better than vanishing., f 58;
#X obj 20 250 r disp;
#X obj 20 300 route in-l in-r status modal modal-off alert led;
#N canvas 40 40 1000 620 levels 0;
#X text 20 20 Two jobs per channel \, both derived once when the level arrives rather than every frame: the bar WIDTH in pixels \, and the 8px readout TEXT. env~ reports 0-100 dB \, the screen is 128 px \, so the scale is 1.28., f 58;
#X obj 20 130 inlet;
#X obj 20 170 list split 1;
#X obj 20 210 i;
#X obj 20 250 t f f;
#X obj 20 310 makefilename %g;
#X obj 20 350 list prepend L;
#X obj 20 390 s \$0-txt-l;
#X obj 220 310 * 1.28;
#X obj 220 350 i;
#X obj 220 390 clip 1 128;
#X obj 220 430 s \$0-w-l;
#X obj 520 130 inlet;
#X obj 520 170 list split 1;
#X obj 520 210 i;
#X obj 520 250 t f f;
#X obj 520 310 makefilename %g;
#X obj 520 350 list prepend R;
#X obj 520 390 s \$0-txt-r;
#X obj 720 310 * 1.28;
#X obj 720 350 i;
#X obj 720 390 clip 1 128;
#X obj 720 430 s \$0-w-r;
#X text 20 480 clip 1 128 matters: gFillArea with a width of 0 is untested on the device and silence is the common case. i before makefilename keeps the readout a whole number., f 58;
