#X connect 14 1 17 0;
#X connect 17 0 18 0;
#X restore 300 500 pd two;
#N canvas 40 40 1000 860 many 0;
#X text 20 20 THREE TO FIVE MOVING -- one 8px line each \, newest at top \, 21 characters wide. More movers than fit is not an error: the oldest simply fall off the end of the list upstream., f 52;
#X obj 20 140 inlet;
#X obj 20 190 t f b;
#X msg 400 230 0;
#X obj 400 280 s \$0-drawctr;
#X obj 20 240 until;
#X obj 20 300 f;
#X obj 160 250 r \$0-drawctr;
#X obj 20 350 t f f;
#X obj 600 400 + 1;
#X obj 600 450 s \$0-drawctr;
#X obj 20 410 t f f;
#X obj 400 470 * 9;
#X obj 400 520 list prepend 2;
#X obj 400 580 list append 8;
#X obj 20 470 text get \$0-params;
#X obj 20 530 list split 1;
#X obj 20 650 list prepend;
#X obj 20 710 s \$0-text;
#X text 20 760 THE COUNTER RESETS BEFORE THE LOOP \, off the rightmost outlet \, and rides a \$0- send rather than a cord back into f's cold inlet -- which would run straight through the arithmetic. Same shape as m_nano's mode toggle., f 52;
#X text 560 640 y is 9 times the row \, so 0 \, 9 \, 18 \, 27 \, 36. Five 8px rows with a pixel between them \, the last ending at 43 -- inside the 46 the param area owns., f 46;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 1 3 0;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 2 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 7 0 6 1;
#X connect 6 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 1 9 0;
#X connect 9 0 10 0;
#X connect 8 0 11 0;
#X connect 11 1 12 0;
#X connect 12 0 13 0;
#X connect 13 0 14 0;
#X connect 14 0 17 1;
#X connect 11 0 15 0;
#X connect 15 0 16 0;
#X connect 16 1 17 0;
#X connect 17 0 18 0;
#X restore 620 500 pd many;
#X text 20 570 select 1 2 \, and the REJECT outlet carries the size straight into pd many -- which is what it needs to know how many rows to draw. Size 0 cannot reach here: pd layers only raises this layer while a parameter is alive., f 58;
#X text 620 570 The meters go out off the rightmost outlet \, before any text \, so the strip is drawn even if a layout branch somehow draws nothing. Signal presence is the one thing that must never disappear., f 46;
#X connect 2 0 3 0;
#X connect 3 1 4 0;
#X connect 3 0 5 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 6 0 7 0;
#X connect 6 1 8 0;
#X connect 6 2 9 0;
#X restore 580 920 pd draw-param;
#N canvas 40 40 1500 700 draw-home 0;
#X text 20 20 THE HOME SCREEN IS THE TWO LEVEL METERS. An 8px readout above each bar so the meters stay calibratable \, the bars and their gate marks from pd meters-big \, and the footer underneath., f 58;
#X obj 20 130 inlet;
#X obj 20 170 t b b b b;
#X msg 20 240 0 0 8;
#X obj 20 290 list append;
#X obj 180 250 r \$0-txt-l;
#X obj 20 340 s \$0-text;
#X msg 340 240 0 27 8;
#X obj 340 290 list append;
#X obj 500 250 r \$0-txt-r;
#X obj 340 340 s \$0-text;
#X obj 660 240 s \$0-meters-big;
#X msg 900 240 0 54 8;
#X obj 900 290 list append;
#X obj 1060 250 r \$0-foot;
#X obj 900 340 s \$0-text;
#X text 20 430 Each text line is a geometry message box -- x \, y \, height -- with the words appended from a receive. pd text-out turns that into gPrintln with a typetag that fits., f 46;
#X text 420 430 The footer holds whatever was last sent as status -- u_init at boot \, then m_nano's mode. Two writers on one bus is the documented model. The selector was called boot until it stopped being only about booting., f 46;
#X text 820 430 Ten OSC messages a frame including the clear and the flip \, against six for the Phase 1 display. The metro period is one number in the parent if the device ever objects., f 46;
#X text 20 560 y 0-7 readout \, 10-21 bar \, 23-25 gate mark \, 27-34 readout \, 37-48 bar \, 50-52 gate mark \, 54-61 footer. 62 of the 64 rows \, and only because the info bar is off -- see ref-display.md., f 58;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 2 3 3 0;
