#X obj 1150 1370 + 1;
#X obj 1150 1420 t f f;
#X obj 1330 1470 s \$0-framestore;
#X obj 1150 1470 s \$0-frame;
#X obj 20 1330 text size \$0-params;
#X obj 20 1390 t f f;
#X obj 700 1450 - 1;
#X obj 700 1500 s \$0-agectr;
#X obj 20 1450 until;
#X obj 20 1510 f;
#X obj 200 1460 r \$0-agectr;
#X obj 20 1570 t f f;
#X obj 700 1610 - 1;
#X obj 700 1660 s \$0-agectr;
#X obj 20 1640 t f f;
#X obj 500 1710 f;
#X obj 20 1710 text get \$0-params 0 1;
#X obj 20 1770 t b f;
#X obj 700 1830 f;
#X obj 860 1790 r \$0-frame;
#X obj 20 1890 -;
#X obj 20 1950 >= 13;
#X obj 20 2000 select 1;
#X obj 500 2060 text delete \$0-params;
#X text 1000 360 THE ORDER IS THE TRIGGER \, right to left: take the frame number \, then the name -- which decides WHICH ROW to write and whether writing is allowed at all -- and only then the value \, which completes the line and commits it., f 40;
#X text 1000 620 ONE moses DECIDES UPDATE-OR-APPEND. text search returns the row for a name already on screen and -1 for one it has never seen -- measured \, not assumed. A hit is the row to overwrite \; a miss falls through to the current size \, which text set treats as an append., f 40;
#X text 1000 1000 THE SIXTH CONTROL IS REFUSED \, not rotated in. Once five rows are live \, a new name is dropped until one ages out -- so nothing ever shifts under your eyes while you are reading it. The cost is honest: move nine faders and you see the five you touched first \, not the five most recent. Rotating instead is what made this unreadable in the first place., f 40;
#X text 20 2120 13 FRAMES \, NOT 12 \, and that is deliberate. pd layers still clears \$0-a-param on a 1200 ms delay \, so the store outlives the flag by one frame. Otherwise a rounding difference could leave the param layer winning with nothing to draw -- a blank screen \, which looks exactly like a dead patch., f 46;
#X text 620 2120 AGEING SCANS \, AND COUNTS DOWN. With rows held in place the expired ones are no longer all at the tail \, so every line is checked -- from the LAST index toward 0 \, because deleting a line shifts everything below it and walking downward is what makes that harmless. until's own count bounds the loop \, so a size of 0 runs it zero times and text get is never handed a line that does not exist -- which ERRORS \, and prints., f 40;
#X obj 20 810 t b;
#X text 620 1000 THE t b IS A BUG FIX. moses's left outlet emits the VALUE it did not match -- the -1 text search returned for a name it has never seen -- and text size passes a float straight through \, so -1 arrived at text set as a line number: error text set: line number (-1) < 0. Second time this shape has bitten: a reject or moses outlet carries data \, never a bang., f 46;
